    {
      "id": "ba403960-5ae3-547c-9466-3822d8cf0528",
      "title": "C, D and E",
      "summary": "Three neighbours: D sits between the two black keys, E just after them.",
      "kind": "concept",
      "minutes": 6,
      "concept": {
        "title": "Three fingers, three keys",
        "paragraphs": [
          "D is the white key between the two black keys. E is the white key just to the right of them.",
          "Fingers are numbered from the thumb: thumb is 1, index is 2, middle is 3. Put 1 on C, 2 on D and 3 on E, and leave them resting there.",
          "Going up the keyboard, notes go up the staff. C sits on its short line, D hangs just under the staff, and E sits on the bottom line."
        ],
        "keys": [
          60,
          62,
          64
        ],
        "tip": "Curve your fingers as if you were holding a small ball. Play with the tips, not the flat pads."
      },
