    {
      "id": "4eb18dd9-6443-5620-9f55-ed8e203c1cce",
      "title": "F and G",
      "summary": "Two more keys, beside the group of three black keys. Your whole hand is now in place.",
      "kind": "concept",
      "minutes": 7,
      "concept": {
        "title": "A hand in five-finger position",
        "paragraphs": [
          "F is the white key just to the left of a group of three black keys. G is the next white key up.",
          "With 1 on C, your fingers 4 and 5 land on F and G. One finger per key, five keys in a row: that is five-finger position.",
          "On the staff, F sits in the bottom space and G on the second line."
        ],
        "keys": [
          60,
          62,
          64,
          65,
          67
        ],
        "tip": "Fingers 4 and 5 are the weakest. Keep them curved and let the weight of your arm do the work."
      },
